  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Republic of the Marshall Islands Partnership for Development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia&apos;s bilateral aid program in the Republic of the Marshall Islands (RMI) focuses on climate resilience; family protection, social inclusion and services; and people, institutions and connections. On climate resilience, Australia directly supports RMI&#x2019;s Climate Change Directorate to implement its National Adaptation Plan. Australia is strengthening family protection, social inclusion and services through supplementary funding for the Pacific Women Lead program, alongside our Direct Aid Program (DAP) grants which reach beyond Majuro to RMI&#x2019;s neighbouring island communities. Finally, Australia is strengthening people, institutions and connections through critical electoral support; funding for the Pacific Media Institute to deliver media workshops; and supporting RMI&#x2019;s Worker&#x2019;s Compensation scheme through an AusP3 adviser.</narrative>
  </description>
